            <ArticleTitle>Thyroid dysfunction and headache.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>51-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An observational study of thyroid function tests performed in patients with headache prior to referral to a neurological clinic found no headache cases attributable to either hypothyroidism or hyperthyroidism. The role of thyroid dysfunction in the aetiology of headache remains uncertain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
